  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></math>&nbsp;is a function defined as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>→</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>19</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></math> is its inverse function, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mn>7</mn></mfenced></math> is equal to&nbsp;"
